(5732222, 833567, 100393, '<td valign="top">II''m giving a mediocre 5, so I''ll let you know why. Although I like the pose and the intensity of the gaze, I''m not at all taken with the composition - perhaps I''m looking at this with an unsophisticated eye but the left eye (your/her left) holds the focus but the centred composition draws the eye away from here to the nose, which because of your depth of field is slightly out of focus. I think this would be a far more effective image if you had place the left eye dead centre.<br/> <br/>Perhaps it was your intention to confound and provoke in this way, perhaps the title alludes to a deliberate unbalancing of the image - but in the final analysis, it isn''t quite working for me.</td>', 'II''m giving a mediocre 5, so I''ll let you know why. Although I like the pose and the intensity of the gaze, I''m not at all taken with the composition - perhaps I''m looking at this with an unsophisticated eye but the left eye (your/her left) holds the focus but the centred composition draws the eye away from here to the nose, which because of your depth of field is slightly out of focus. I think this would be a far more effective image if you had place the left eye dead centre. Perhaps it was your intention to confound and provoke in this way, perhaps the title alludes to a deliberate unbalancing of the image - but in the final analysis, it isn''t quite working for me.', '2009-11-18 12:19:46.000000', NULL, 1),
