(5741348, 834184, 30861, '<td valign="top">"Perhaps this is what the "suffering" guy above was thinking? No understanding a narrow depth of field/focus?"<br/> <br/>**************<br/> <br/>Maybe, but here''s another theory; some people, using LCD monitors, have set them to other-than-designed resolutions, and they cannot handle that. The result is messy artifacting, and it can REALLY mess up when you have a fine grid like that window screen. <br/> <br/>So that may be your answer.<br/> <br/>Cool shot, BTW; love it!</td>', '"Perhaps this is what the "suffering" guy above was thinking? No understanding a narrow depth of field/focus?" ************** Maybe, but here''s another theory; some people, using LCD monitors, have set them to other-than-designed resolutions, and they cannot handle that. The result is messy artifacting, and it can REALLY mess up when you have a fine grid like that window screen.  So that may be your answer. Cool shot, BTW; love it!', '2009-11-25 10:35:55.000000', NULL, 0),
