(5741618, 833146, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Debbi:</b></div><hr/><i> How do you get them to stay put ? LOL<br/>When I try they always fly away<br/>Any secrets? Great detail in the eyes!<br/>Debbi </i></td></tr></table> <br/>most of them do fly away but i get the occasional one that will pose for pics .. !!<br/>be very fast on the shutter when you''ve got them in focus .. always manual focus .. using am external flash helps immensely .. take heaps of shots coz at this magnification its very difficult to get the focus exactly where you want it .. mostly you wont know until you see them on the monitor ..  approach them very slowly .. most of them will fly away if your shadow falls on them .. etc .. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Debbi: How do you get them to stay put ? LOLWhen I try they always fly awayAny secrets? Great detail in the eyes!Debbi  most of them do fly away but i get the occasional one that will pose for pics .. !!be very fast on the shutter when you''ve got them in focus .. always manual focus .. using am external flash helps immensely .. take heaps of shots coz at this magnification its very difficult to get the focus exactly where you want it .. mostly you wont know until you see them on the monitor ..  approach them very slowly .. most of them will fly away if your shadow falls on them .. etc .. :)', '2009-11-25 13:31:37.000000', NULL, 0),
